# The cell is a coordinate. The loop also holds max |dE/dA| to the problem force norm. Python periodic_sqnm is given -dE/dA.
# Variable-cell SQNM on the Morse pair potential. The cell is a coordinate. The atomic force uses the problem L2 stop, and the max-norm of dE/dA uses that same number. Python periodic_sqnm multiplies the supplied lattice derivative by -1, so the harness passes -dE/dA and the step descends. lattice_weight is 2. The call goes through aseOptimizer with vc_relax true. The calculator stress is (dE/dA) A^T / det(A), so the wrapper's deralat equals -dE/dA. Tuned row: history length 20. eps_subsp stays 1e-5.
